description:
Who We Are: Phoenix Engineering Group is a leader in broadband technologies and infrastructure, boasting a robust portfolio of projects across Germany, Greece, and the Netherlands. We cater to the diverse needs of telecom and infrastructure providers throughout Europe, offering comprehensive services for project implementation.
Our Culture: At Phoenix Engineering, we fuse the strength of a formidable group of companies with the energetic spirit of a dynamic and youthful team. We cultivate a culture grounded in teamwork, mutual support, and the relentless pursuit of excellence. We celebrate achievements, stand united during challenges, and are committed to fostering the growth and success of every team member.
Your Role: As a Quality Assurance Engineer you will be responsible for ensuring that the department's deliverables meet quality standards, and conducting audits and tests to identify and resolve quality issues.
How You Will Contribute to Our Success:

Conduct audits and tests;
Ensure proper planning and direction of the operational functions;
Document and analyze quality data;
Employ Python scripts to automate quality checks and streamline workflow processes;
Develop and implement quality control procedures;
Investigate root causes of quality issues;
Provide training to employees;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams.

To be a fit you will need:

Bachelor’s Degree in Engineering, Telecommunications, Computer Science or another related technical field;
2 years previous experience in telecommunication or operations field;
Excellent knowledge of QGIS/ArcGIS or other similar design and visualization software;
Advanced MS Office skills;
Excellent command of the English language;
Good communication skills;.
Excellent time management and organization skills with a strong problem-solving mindset.

Ideally you should also have:

Knowledge of programming languages (preferably python & SQL);
Previous working experience in FTTx projects;
German language knowledge (current level B2).

What we offer:

Competitive remuneration package.
Active participation in exciting and challenging projects that shape the infrastructure of the future.
Opportunities for skill development and career advancement through theoretical and on-the-job training.
Other corporate benefits.

Phoenix Engineering is an equal opportunity employer committed to diversity and inclusion. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds and experiences, treating them with fairness and confidentiality. We do not discriminate based on age, sex, race, color, religion, national origin, disability, or any other characteristic. If you're ready to unlock your potential, we eagerly await your CV!

